{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/107288-declaration-phase-who-uses-it","id":107288,"title":"Declaration Phase: Who uses it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-07T00:12:19-07:00","id":107288,"title":"Declaration Phase: Who uses it?","content":"In theory, I understand the purpose of the declaration phase: When the players roll initiative, lowest declare first and highest declares last. Then highest acts first, and lowest goes last. Changing your acfion is often possible (if not limited), but may require a penalty to do so. However, for all of the games (WoD and others) that use this rule as part if its initiative rules, my group as never used them. Actually, we sometimes try, but it adds another layer to combat that just makes the combat even slower, and it only lasts one round before we just go back to our default; Roll initiatve, highest declares and acts on it. So, I'm curious how many use the Declaration phase, if it's used as-written, modified, or in special circumstances, and how many have also abandoned the Declaration phase as it's written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T00:25:47-07:00","id":107296,"title":"","content":"In every game I played we used the Declaration phase as written.<br /> It was never a problem or a complication to us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T00:36:06-07:00","id":107303,"title":"","content":"In Mage I do it as written. In the odd event that combat comes up that is actually not so lopsided that there is actual relevance in who goes first. But with Mage, either they are unprepared, and therefore get stomped, or they did prepare, and they do the stomping.<br /> <br /> In Vampire, the group has gotten over their D&amp;D mentality, and therefore, I use it.<br /> <br /> In Werewolf, however, going through the initiative phase twice makes the combat slow down too much for how often combat happens in Werewolf. Therefore, we don't use it, instead going as you said. However, I do still give my players description based on the NPC's actions as they are intending to do, therefore giving the players who are going to be attacked knowledge of the incoming blow or whatnot, so they can 'abort action' with no penalty if they want to defend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><i>&quot;Maturity is knowing you were an idiot in the past.&quot;<br /> &quot;If that's true, then Wisdom is knowing you'll be an idiot in the future.&quot;<br /> &quot;And Common Sense is knowing that you should try not to be an idiot NOW.&quot;<br /> -Questionable Content 976</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1042-zhyzhaksmate","name":"ZhyzhaksMate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1042_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T00:37:07-07:00","id":107304,"title":"","content":"When running the cWOD, I usually use it.<br /> <br /> Most of the presentations of it don't really add much to the flow of combat to have to do so. It does give a large advantage to going first, but since initiative is re-rolled every round, it isn't like you can setup multiple turn effects reliably enough to really play around with that advantage. It can also lead to some &quot;decision lock&quot; for lower init players that don't know what to do because they're characters are in a reactive mode.<br /> <br /> However, I usually run with the DA Revised way of handling it. It doesn't completely justify the declaration phase, but it has a much better handling of multiple actions, which can at least help reduce the decision lock aspect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-07T21:17:34-07:00","id":107960,"title":"","content":"Basically never.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T00:34:30-07:00","id":108018,"title":"","content":"Best part of cWoD combat system. I use the DA version in all my games, and have no problem at all. The transition from &quot;D&amp;D&quot; initiative was tough for a while some 10-15 years ago, I suppose, but it's been a while, so hard to remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T08:21:41-07:00","id":108209,"title":"","content":"The closest I've seen to anyone even trying a &quot;Declaration Phase&quot; is when a friend of mine would run initiative from the bottom up. So the lowest Initiative Score declares their action, and anyone who wants to pre-empt that Action can do so. Otherwise, they just resolve it. It works OK as long as Combat has only two sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-08T08:30:40-07:00","id":108217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/107288-declaration-phase-who-uses-it?p=108209#post108209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The closest I've seen to anyone even trying a &quot;Declaration Phase&quot; is when a friend of mine would run initiative from the bottom up. So the lowest Initiative Score declares their action, and anyone who wants to pre-empt that Action can do so. Otherwise, they just resolve it. It works OK as long as Combat has only two sides.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used it when I ran Aberrant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T04:13:55-07:00","id":109158,"title":"","content":"I've always used it. I find it greatly preferable to D&amp;D style initiative. It means that a lower initiative does not become an advantage, as it can for certain builds in other systems. The Declaration phase is necessary to the whole system for combat. Otherwise, lower initiatives gain significant advantage (namely getting to react to what is happening), and there should not be a benefit for being worse at something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"<a href=http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png target=_blank>http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png</a>\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2323-killersquirrel59","name":"killersquirrel59","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"558"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T06:13:47-07:00","id":109224,"title":"","content":"When I played in Werewolf it was used but only half the time depending upon the combat situation and who was the ST. In Mage I've never used it because both of my Mage characters do their damnedest to avoid direct combat. One character is just Really bad at it and my other character tends to do the unexpected with a single action and ends the conflict right then and there. Or he runs away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-09T08:17:21-07:00","id":109308,"title":"","content":"I use it and like it pretty much. It's very efficient if the group's efficient in taking decisions and the players with the highest initiative get a view of the whole situation before taking a decision which is awesome, it allows for interruptions and saves too. At first it looks wonky though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>former lightmaguz","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/514-auron","name":"Auron","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T08:26:09-07:00","id":110098,"title":"","content":"Never used it. It began as a general lack of awareness of the rules that later evolved into routine. I'm not the most rules oriented guy, and I get set in my ways, even when I'm not doing something right. But I've always wanted to try it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T10:31:51-07:00","id":110155,"title":"","content":"My players are fairly new to cWoD.. only recently have they gotten the routine of the declaration stage down with lots of reminders and it helps if i keep track of what round (This is still round 2 guys, Rage Furry Anger hasn't gone yet). I agree with the above saying it's a pain in WtA because of the rage actions at the end, but my pack hates to frenzy so you rarely get more than 2 of them burning rage in the same round.<br /> <br /> However, I have yet to find an initiative system in any game that makes me go &quot;Yes! This is it, this is the best initiative system!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2693-agentunicorn","name":"AgentUnicorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T11:00:32-07:00","id":110176,"title":"","content":"Hopefully not to beat the horse too dead, but if you're having trouble with Rage actions, check up the free Dark Ages core rules. It is, in my view, the only cWOD combat system that actually bothered taking multiple actions into account properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-10T11:10:53-07:00","id":110182,"title":"","content":"I wholeheartedly agree with the above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T20:07:37-07:00","id":145185,"title":"","content":"I played with it back in my old group in AZ. Now-a-days we are too used to Pathfinder to bother with it, and my player's don't really get too much advantage out of going lower in the initiative. Combat generally should be about reacting to whoever acts first anyway. The second person to draw is usually the one who gets the shot off first =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T09:12:35-07:00","id":145727,"title":"","content":"I typically use it in one form or another. It's handy for ordering Rage spending and determining dice pools. Normally I simply go with How much Rage are you spending, how many actions are you splitting for, are any of them defensive?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T09:31:15-07:00","id":145742,"title":"","content":"Not as written. I know the intent of lower initiative declares first, but I think that those who go first should have to fly blind. If they want to study their opponent's actions, split the die pool and do a Perception check as well. This also generally speeds up action resolution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3078-coffee-zombie","name":"Coffee Zombie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T00:34:56-07:00","id":150093,"title":"","content":"It depends on the situation.<br /> <br /> There are more than 4 combatants and half of 'em have 3+ multiple actions through powers and splitting? Screw declaration phase! It takes too long.<br /> <br /> We have a climactic duell between a character and his nemesis? Even if they both have 1000 actions each, declaration phase is important.<br /> <br /> Multiple combatants all with only one action (with options to split not more than once because of the dice-pools)? Yeah go on declaration phase, characters only have one action and they hate to waste it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}